# System Architecture — Mermaid Diagrams

`can-logger-decoder` v2.0.0 · Day 3 Architecture Guide

This file contains Mermaid diagrams illustrating the system architecture and
the end-to-end flow of CAN frames from hardware/vcan sources through the
parser, state machine, DBC decoder, and logger output.

Render these with any Mermaid-compatible viewer (GitHub, GitLab, VS Code
Mermaid preview, Mermaid Live Editor, or `mermaid-cli`).

---

## Diagram 1 — End-to-end data flow

Frame journey from source ingestion to logger output.

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    %% ===== Inputs =====
    subgraph IN["Frame Sources"]
        PHYS[Physical CAN<br/>MCP2515 via SPI]
        VIRT[Virtual CAN<br/>SocketCAN vcan0 / can0]
        MOCK[Mock Telemetry<br/>physics-based simulator]
    end

    %% ===== Pipeline =====
    subgraph PIPE["Decode Pipeline"]
        INGEST[can_bus_read()<br/>frame ingestion<br/>can_parser.c]
        VALIDATE[DLC & ID validation<br/>can_core.c · dlc_validator.c]
        STATE[Error state machine<br/>src/state/<br/>warning → passive → bus-off]
        FILTER[Acceptance filtering<br/>can_filters.c]
        DECODE[DBC signal decode<br/>dbc_decoder.c<br/>Intel/Motorola · scale+offset]
    end

    %% ===== Outputs =====
    subgraph OUT["Logger Outputs"]
        DASH[Live terminal dashboard<br/>ANSI colorized gauges]
        CSV[CSV telemetry log<br/>can_log.csv]
        METRICS[Runtime metrics<br/>src/utils/metrics.c]
    end

    %% Flow
    PHYS --> INGEST
    VIRT --> INGEST
    MOCK --> INGEST

    INGEST --> VALIDATE
    VALIDATE --> STATE
    STATE --> FILTER
    FILTER --> DECODE

    DECODE --> DASH
    DECODE --> CSV
    DECODE --> METRICS

    %% Fault side-path
    STATE -.->|BUS_OFF / SPI fault| BOR[Bus-off recovery<br/>128 recessive bits<br/>reset → rejoin]
    BOR -.->|recovered| STATE

    %% Styling
    classDef input fill:#e1f5e1,stroke:#2e7d32;
    classDef pipe fill:#e3f2fd,stroke:#1565c0;
    classDef out fill:#fff3e0,stroke:#ef6c00;
    classDef fault fill:#ffebee,stroke:#c62828,stroke-dasharray: 5 5;

    class PHYS,VIRT,MOCK input;
    class INGEST,VALIDATE,STATE,FILTER,DECODE pipe;
    class DASH,CSV,METRICS out;
    class BOR fault;
```

