## Diagram 2 — Frame reception sequence

Sequence of a single received CAN frame through the stack.

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant HW as MCP2515 Hardware
    participant SPI as SPI Driver<br/>src/hardware
    participant P as CAN Parser<br/>src/core/can_parser.c
    participant S as State Machine<br/>src/state/error_machine.c
    participant D as DBC Decoder<br/>src/dbc_decoder.c
    participant L as CSV Logger<br/>src/main.c · logger.c
    participant C as Console<br/>Live dashboard

    HW->>SPI: /INT asserted (frame / error pending)
    SPI->>SPI: Read CANINTF → classify RX / TX / error
    SPI->>P: Deliver can_frame_t (ID, DLC, data)
    P->>P: Strip flag bits; derive is_extended / is_rtr / is_error
    P->>P: Validate DLC (0–8) + ISO-8601 timestamp
    P->>S: Feed frame to error machine
    S-->>P: State: NORMAL / WARNING / BUS_OFF / RESET

    alt Healthy frame
        P->>D: Match DBC message by clean CAN ID
        D->>D: Unpack bits (Intel little / Motorola big)
        D->>D: Apply scale + offset; range check
        D->>L: Emit decoded signal values
        D->>C: Render ANSI dashboard row
        L->>L: Append row to can_log.csv
    else Bus-off / fault
        S->>S: Increment TEC/REC; enter BUS_OFF (TEC > 255)
        S->>L: Log fault event
        S->>S: Trigger bus-off recovery (128 recessive bits)
        S-->>P: RECOVERED → resume frame delivery
    end
```
